This program depends on and bundles/invokes the `mkpfs` library at
runtime:

    Project:    MkPFS
    Source:     https://github.com/PSBrew/MkPFS
    Version:    0.0.8 (at time of writing; run `mkpfs-worker -V` for
                the version actually installed)
    License:    GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)

mkpfs-worker exists specifically so that closed-source callers never
need to `import mkpfs` directly: they invoke this tool as a separate
subprocess and exchange CLI arguments / stdout / files, which is the
GPL boundary this project is designed to sit on.
